# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# The refresh-rate page on the device itself (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.safari). SpringBoard
# refuses a file:// URL handed to it by another process ("it REFUSES"), so the page
# is served on loopback instead -- which needs no radio -- and opened as an http URL,
# the same way rc.jobs.safari opens yandex.ru on a port with Wi-Fi. webserve keeps
# running (the trailing & is run_rc's "do not wait") so reloads work; it says each
# request on the console, which is how the log tells "Safari never asked" from
# "Safari asked and WebKit did not paint".
/redwood/bin/webserve /redwood/share/web 8080 &
/redwood/bin/net_test show
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/battery_test open http://127.0.0.1:8080/
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn SAFARI_OPEN
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 60
/bin/ps -A
